WEBVTT

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:03.957
Every pursuit starts on SAM.gov.

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:06.517
Rivet monitors new federal opportunities

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:08.837
with the filters set for your firm,

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:11.137
pulls in the solicitation documents,

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:14.857
and analyzes each one against your capabilities.

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:19.010
So you start with work that fits, and a clear reason why.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.787
Those opportunities land in your pipeline.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.807
You can see what’s been analyzed,

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.167
what’s moving into proposal preparation,

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.750
and what’s been submitted.

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:32.570
Deadlines and fit scores show you where to focus.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.557
Open a pursuit to see the AI’s analysis.

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:40.197
It reads the solicitation, pulls out the requirements,

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:43.357
and compares them with your firm’s experience.

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:45.137
You get a bid recommendation,

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:48.440
with the strengths and gaps laid out for your review.

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.247
In Selection, Rivet recommends

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:54.097
past projects from your firm’s records,

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:56.453
each with the experience that supports it.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:01.167
Then it recommends the people whose qualifications fit each role.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.603
Accept the team, or compare an alternative.

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:08.117
Those choices build your experience matrix,

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:11.100
connecting people to the projects they delivered.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:14.460
Approve it, and the selection moves forward.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:20.497
From there, Rivet drafts resumes, project sheets, and narratives.

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.697
The solicitation, amendments,

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:25.797
and generated sections stay side by side,

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:28.590
so you can check the source against the output.

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:35.007
The Proposal tab brings every section into one SF330 package.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:39.340
See what’s ready, fill any gaps, and give it your final review.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:41.437
Want something changed?

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:43.127
Just tell the assistant.

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:46.797
Rivet saves your feedback on tone, terminology,

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.847
and how you describe your work,

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.430
and uses it to guide future drafts.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:56.317
Your pursue and decline decisions sharpen the scoring, too.

00:01:56.350 --> 00:02:00.390
So with every pursuit, the writing sounds more like your team.

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:03.787
Behind it all is your firm’s knowledge base:

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:07.277
past projects, personnel and their qualifications,

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:09.400
and the partner firms you team with.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:12.237
New files come in through Documents,

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:15.380
where you upload records and follow their processing.

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:17.337
That’s Rivet.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:21.697
Monitoring, analysis, matching, and proposal preparation,

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:25.448
handled for you, with your team in control of every decision.
